{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01KEA7XaLuSt5L4vse2jrany","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed predicted data for each planned experiment in the experiment_plan, under the \"best\" tier assumptions. I need to provide result_rationale for each prediction explaining why we'd get those results under the best-case scenario.\n\nLet me go through each planned experiment and generate predictions consistent with the best tier definition:\n\n**Best tier definition:**\n- exp-001 confirms d012 signal at scale with significance\n- Cross-family C0 pattern replicates cleanly\n- MaxSAT ablation shows clear satisfiability value\n\n**Key metric ranges:**\n\n\nNow I'm looking at the expected performance ranges for each metric under best-case conditions—folio gap improvements, combined gap reductions, statistical significance thresholds, and cross-model replication rates across the different model families, plus the tiebreak win rate expectations.\n\nThe narrative confirms all three core claims hold up: SICA delivers meaningful tiebreaking improvements, C0 functions as a validated continuous predictor across multiple architectures, and MaxSAT satisfiability checking proves essential. The scatter plot shows a clean monotonic relationship between C0 scores and performance gaps.\n\nI'm tracking the experiment pipeline—the first run is already underway with 804 questions split between PW and FOLIO, and the next phase will test K sensitivity across the ablation space.\n\nNow I'm mapping out the remaining experiments: tiebreak baseline analysis is partially complete, then I need to validate C0 diagnostics on CPU, test scaling across 7B and 8B models, run the 32B QwQ regime analysis, and work through constraint quality case studies and overhead measurements.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_in